  "decision_date": "22/06/2007",
  "description": "Change of use from offices to a 96 bedroom hotel, with ancillary meeting rooms cafe and lounge; enlargement of ground floor comprising of a front lean - to addition and infilling of undercroft; erection of a fifth floor, and external alterations thereto.",
  "site_name": "8-10",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "24/06/2007",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": "TW3 1JL",
  "street_name": "Lampton Road",
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Major dwellings",
  "lapsed_date": "21/06/2010",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the extension hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building.",
    "Condition : 3 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 4 - No fans, louvres, ducts or other external plant shall be installed without the prior approval of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 5 - No deliveries shall be taken at or despatched from the site outside the hours of 8am to 8pm.\r\n",
    "Condition : 6 - Notwithstanding the information contained in the application, details of a parking layout shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority before the occupation of the approved use.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with approved details.\r\n\r\n",
    "Condition : 7 - Details of disabled access to the premises and details of disabled toilet facilities shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the occupation of the approved use.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with approved details.\r\n",
    "Condition : 8 - Details of any fume extraction equipment, including details of sound attenuation for any necessary plant, which may be required for the caf? ancillary to the hotel shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with approved details.\r\n\r\nReason:  In order that the Local Planning Authority may be satisfied as to the arrangements for preventing loss of amenity to neighbouring premises due to fumes and smells.",
    "Condition : 9 - The caf? use shall be ancillary to the main hotel use and shall be confined to sales to customers residing at the hotel.\r\n",
    "Condition : 10 - The developer shall submit a Green Travel Plan and Car Park Management Plan for approval to the Local Planning Authority and these plans shall be approved in writing prior to first occupation of any of the development.  The Green Travel Plan shall cover, but is not limited to, the activities of end users, staff, trainees including both construction and hospitality training. \r\n",
    "Condition : 11 - Further details of agreements for local training as outlined in the submitted letter dated 20th June 2007 from Kensington College of Business are to be provided prior to occupation of the development.  Such details shall include, but are not limited to measures designed to encourage links with the local community.  Such details are to be complied with following occupation. \r\n"
  ],
